6ede2c9e (3214 1792934576525 "guenchi" (("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f350") (src . "test: the interleave row waits for the search's answer, not for a time\n\nThe D-interleave row of unreadable-acknowledge-routes waited twenty\nseconds, counted as 200 shell sleeps, for a hold mark the search never\nproduces, then released the held export. The count is not a clock: on a\nslow runner it took about thirty seconds, the daemon's hold expired on\nits own (THEOURGIA_HOLD_MS, default 30000), the client's 30 s read\ntimeout ended the export with transport-unknown, and the fold the daemon\nruns next left its own hold mark inside the window, read as a held\nsearch. Reproduced on the development machine with eleven seconds added\nbefore the search.\n\nThe row now waits for the search's answer on the monotonic clock\n(trace-poll.ss, bound 20 s), reads whether a hold is acknowledged at\nthat instant, and only then releases the export; the daemon holds for up\nto 120 s, above every wait, and the row asserts no hold-expired line in\nthe serve log. On a red the serve log's tail and both clients' output\nand standard error are printed under the row. A control with a second\nexport in the search's place reads red through the new answered flag.\n\n- test/unreadable-acknowledge-routes.sc: the row, the two helpers, the\n  load of trace-poll.ss.\n- test/rows-baseline.txt: the fixture's line (68 rows, 77 lines, md5).\n- test/RUN.md: the fixture named among trace-poll.ss's loaders.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 474))))
